 1174 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: The SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio now supports multitenancy, allowing HDI container service instances to be managed via SAP HANA Cloud tenants. The SAP HANA project explorer enables binding database applications to tenant containers of type \"hdi\" and \"schema\".  See:  Bind Applications to Database Services with SAP HANA Projects Explorer  Bind an Application to an SAP HANA Cloud Multitenant HDI Container  Deploy Artifacts with the SAP HANA Projects Explorer.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-24\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: T2502b\n\n--- Record 1175 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, you can upgrade the .hdiconfig file for SAP HANA Cloud database modules using the context menu in the SAP HANA Project Explorer or the Explorer tree view of the SAP Business Application Studio.  See: Upgrading the SAP HDI Container Configuration File.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-24\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: T2502b\n\n--- Record 1176 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, you can now use the Virtual Table Editor to fetch the latest column definitions from the remote source, ensuring that your virtual table reflects any changes to the column structure in the remote database.  See: Create Virtual Tables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-24\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: T2502b\n\n--- Record 1177 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SAP HANA Development Tooling  SAP Build Code\nDescription: In the SAP HANA Native Application dev space for SAP Business Application Studio, you can now use the generative-AI tools included in SAP Build Code to generate SQL statements in the SQL console that use customer-defined data models.  See: Use a Custom Data Model for AI-Powered SQL Generation  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-24\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: T2502b\n\n--- Record 1178 ---\nComponent: SAP Document AI\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Google Cloud Region\nDescription: SAP Document AI is now available in the Google Cloud region in30 - India (Mumbai).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Intelligent Technologies\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-15\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1179 ---\nComponent: UI Theme Designer\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Theming Base Content for CF and Neo.\nDescription: The base theming content is updated to version 11.28.2. Review the changes at https://github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1180 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Calculation Views\nDescription: In the calculation view editor, you can now create derived variables that dynamically retrieve values from", "github.com/SAP/theming-base-content/releases.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-03-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1180 ---\nComponent: SAP Business Application Studio\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Calculation Views\nDescription: In the calculation view editor, you can now create derived variables that dynamically retrieve values from a selected data source at runtime. Unlike user-provided variables, which require manual input, derived variables are automatically supplied with values by the selected data source.  See Create Variables.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-18\nValid as Of: 2025-03-23\nVersion: T2502b\n\n", "--- Record 3951 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deprecation of Weak Client Certificate Chains\nDescription: This is a reminder that, as originally announced on May 18, 2023, we plan to harden the security standards on certain properties for client certificates and their certificate chains in November 2023 to further strengthen platform security.   We will do so by raising the OpenSSL security level to 2. This will result in weak certificates or certificate chains no longer being accepted by the platform. For more information and a full definition of security level 2, see https://help.sap.com/docs/link-disclaimer?site=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.openssl.org%2Fdocs%2Fman3.0%2Fman3%2FSSL_CTX_set_security_level.html%23DEFAULT-CALLBACK-BEHAVIOUR  The change will be rolled out gradually, starting with the region br10 on November 29 and the region eu20 on November 30, 2023. All other regions are planned to be updated in January 2024. Further details regarding the timelines for the remaining regions will be announced through this channel in a timely manner.  Note that this change only affects client certificates. If you do not use client certificates / mTLS to authenticate with the platform, you are not affected.  If you are using client certificates / mTLS, you can check your certificate chain using the following command:openssl verify -auth_level=2 -CAfile ./ca.pem -untrusted ./intermediate.pem ./cert.pem  For more details on the command, see SAP Note 3333978 .  Action:  Please contact the issuer of the certificate with the command you executed and the output you got and request a certificate that passes the verification.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3952 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Removal of .NET, Ruby, and R Buildpacks\nDescription: This the final reminder that the .NET, Ruby, and R offline buildpacks have been deprecated and are scheduled to be removed from the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry environment on November 16, 2023.  If you want to continue using these buildpacks after their removal, you can use the online community buildpacks by specifying their URLs in the code of your applications. For more information, see SAP Note 3364781 \nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3953 ---\nComponent: Region\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Additional NAT and LB IPs Added to Amazon Web Services Regions\nDescription: Additional NAT and Load Balancer (LB) IP addresses were added on SAP BTP regions running on Amazon Web Services (AWS). The following regions are affected by this change:        br10 – Brazil (São Paulo)    jp10 – Japan (Tokyo)  ap10 – Australia (Sydney)  ap11 – Asia Pacific (Singapore)  ap12 – Asia Pacific (Seoul)  ca10 – Canada (Montreal)  eu10 – Europe (Frankfurt)  eu11 – Europe (Frankfurt)  us10 – US East (VA)      Action:  If your Cloud Foundry application connects to systems which restrict access by allowlisting IPs in firewall rules, make sure to adopt your configuration accordingly. The new IP addresses may be used at the end of Q1, 2024.   For details, see Regions and API Endpoints for the Cloud Foundry Environment.  In case of questions please contact SAP Support.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3954 ---\nComponent: Service Manager\nEnvironment: Kubernetes\nTitle: SAP BTP Service Operator - Fixed SAP Kubernetes Service Binding Specification\nDescription: The Secret created for the service binding contains an instance name key in the service instance info section. This key uses the BTP name of the service binding, which is the value of the external_name property in the service binding spec. The external_instance_name key has been removed from the secret. For more info, see Formats of Secret Objects.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-11\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3955 ---\nComponent: Java Server\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 8\nDescription: Java Web Tomcat 8 (runtime version 3.190) has been updated to Tomcat version 8.5.95. The new version contains security fixes.   See the Changelog.  Recommended action: Update your applications to the latet runtime version.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3956 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Limits for Roles, Role Collections, Trust, and Service Broker Instances\nDescription: There are limits that apply when you define", " latet runtime version.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3956 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: Limits for Roles, Role Collections, Trust, and Service Broker Instances\nDescription: There are limits that apply when you define roles, role collections, and trust configurations. Furthermore, the number of service broker instances is limited.  For more information, see Limits for Technical Artifacts of the SAP Authorization and Trust Management Service.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-19\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3957 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI Content Assistant (Beta)\nDescription: You can now bootstrap your command and generate fully working DevOps and SRE automation flows by using the new generative AI feature integrated into SAP Automation Pilot. This is a beta feature. See Generative AI in SAP Automation Pilot (Beta).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3958 ---\nComponent: Automation Pilot\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Expression Functions\nDescription: Automation Pilot now supports the jq functions sub and gsub. See Dynamic Expression.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3959 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Application Development in Authorization Management\nDescription: Developers can use the developer tools of administration management. They build their own applications with authorization policies. Administrators assign authorization policies to users, change the rules and attribute values of existing policies, and create new authorization policies. See Configuring Authorization Policies.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3960 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Customer Documents\nDescription: Tenant administrator can upload terms of use and privacy policy documents, and e-mail templates in Thai, Malay and Vietnamese. See Configuring Terms of Use, Configuring Privacy Policies, and Configuring Email Templates.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-11-02\nValid as Of: 2023-11-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 821 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Going forward, users will need an orchestration deployment to use the Prompt Editor and Chat apps.  You likely already have an orchestration deployment running. You can check by viewing your deployments in the ML Ops app. For more information, see View a Deployment.  To create a new orchestration deployment, see Create a Deployment for Orchestration.  Alternatively, administrators can use the Enable Orchestration button available through the interface. \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-19\nValid as Of: 2025-05-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 822 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: New models are supported, including OpenAI GPT, o3, o4-mini, 4.1, 4.1-mini, 4.1-nano and Mistral small instruct.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-19\nValid as Of: 2025-05-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 823 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Image as input is supported in orchestration. For more information, see Templating.  To see which models support image input, consult the model library. For more information, see Model Library.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-19\nValid as Of: 2025-05-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 824 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: New models are supported, including OpenAI GPT, o3, o4-mini, 4.1, 4.1-mini, 4.1-nano and Mistral small instruct.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-19\nValid as Of: 2025-05-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 825 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Studio Home Application\nDescription: You can configure the Studio Home application to allow users to access business process projects outside of the lobby and manage specific artifacts, such as decisions.See Configure the Studio Home Application and Use Studio Home.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-19\nValid as Of: 2025-05-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 826 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changes to Setup for SAP Build Process Automation Integration\nDescription: With an adjustment regarding environment settings on the side of SAP Build Process Automation, the integration between SAP Advanced Financial Closing and SAP Build Process Automation also needs to be adjusted.  As of now the integration will be set up using a destination created in the SAP BTP cockpit. This destination is then maintained in the system settings in SAP Advanced Financial Closing. This new approach replaces the previous out-of-the-box approach that was based on the fact that both tenants were part of the same subaccount.  This change has the benefit that for the integration to work, the subscription for the SAP Build Process Automation tenant no longer has to be part of the same SAP BTP subaccount as the one for SAP Advanced Financial Closing.  More information:How to Set Up the SAP Build Process Automation Integration for SAP Advanced Financial Closing    Area affected: Integration with SAP Build Process Automation  Action: If you've set up the integration with SAP Build Process Automation with the previous approach, you need to adjust the set up to the new approach. This includes the adjustment of the destination in the SAP BTP cockpit and a new connection setup in the Specify Communication Systems app in SAP Advanced Financial Closing.  You can find the information about the destination settings in the SAP Build Process Automation documentation. We've provided links to that documentation and information about the adjustments required in SAP Advanced Financial Closing under How to Set Up the SAP Build Process Automation Integration for SAP Advanced Financial Closing.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-18\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 827 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Move Tasks in Task List Templates\nDescription: You can now move tasks across folders in the closing structure of task list templates. This allows for a more flexible task list management.  More information:  How to Move Tasks  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 828 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Notification Scenario for Financial Close Workflow\nDescription: The new notification scenario Processed Task Approved is now available. This means that users can now receive an email as soon as a task they're assigned to is approved.  More information:  Notifications in the Financial Close Workflow  App affected: ", "-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 828 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Notification Scenario for Financial Close Workflow\nDescription: The new notification scenario Processed Task Approved is now available. This means that users can now receive an email as soon as a task they're assigned to is approved.  More information:  Notifications in the Financial Close Workflow  App affected:  Manage Email Notification Configurations\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 829 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Organizational Units in Email Notifications\nDescription: Email notifications now include organizational units, such as company codes, allowing users to quickly identify affected units.  Area affected: Email notifications\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 830 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Secondary Communication System Information for Workflows\nDescription: In the Create Task from Workflow dialog, you can now add a new column called Secondary Communication System. The secondary communication system helps identify the origin of the workflows. This information is particularly useful when tasks from multiple external systems have identical names. It ensures that you can distinguish between tasks based on their source.  More information:  App affected:  Manage Closing Task Lists\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-05\nValid as Of: 2025-05-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 3081 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for Key Pair Authentication for Snowflake Databases\nDescription: You can now enhance security for a Snowflake connection using key pair authentication. When you configure the connection in the dataflow designer, choose key pair authentication and provide a key file, which can be either encrypted or not encrypted. For more information about the Snowflake connection, see Snowflake in the Administration Guide.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3082 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Upcoming Javascript Change Requires Customer Action:\nDescription: Due to a new Javascript interpreter version that will be introduced in an upcoming patch for SAP Data Intelligence Cloud, operators based on the Javascript \"Message Operator\" or generated from the OpenAPI server template will need to have their scripts adjusted. Customers are advised to update their graphs as soon as possible.  For more information, see 3457456 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3083 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updated Go Libraries\nDescription: The libraries used by the Go operators have been updated. To avoid issues, custom operators or Go scripts using the same libraries as SAP Data Intelligence standard content should match the new versions. For details, refer to the file \"/files/vflow/operators/com/sap/system/golangExecutor2/depmap.json\" in the SAP Data Intelligence repository.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3084 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updated Kafka Operators\nDescription: The library used by the Kafka operators has been updated. This changes the default protocol version to 2.1.0 in anticipation of Kafka release 4.0 dropping support for older versions. Customers are encouraged to update their old Kafka setups or explicitly set the version in the operator configuration to retain compatibility.  For more information, see 3423165  and https://community.sap.com/t5/technology-blogs-by-sap/sap-datasphere-and-sap-data-intelligence-cloud-what-does-this-mean-for-me/ba-p/13603947 on the SAP Community website.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3085 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updated R Versions and Libraries Used by rClient3 and rClient4 Operators\nDescription: The R version used by operators rClient3 and rClient4 has been updated from 3.5.0 to 3.6.3 and 4.1.0 to 4.3.2, respectively. The following R libraries also have been updated: Rserve (to version 1.8-10), jsonlite (to version 1.8.5), tree (to version 1.0-42).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3086 ---\nComponent: SAP Data Intelligence\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: View and Configure Default Resources Requirements for Graphs in the Modeler\nDescription: You can now view the default resource limits for a graph in the Resources section of the Configuration panel in the Modeler. Hover your mouse over the Information icon next to the Resources heading. You can change the limits in the Configuration panel for the current graph. Previously, if tenant administrators didn't specify resource requirements during graph design, the backend service set the default resource requirements for graphs. This new feature provides tenant administrators more control over the resource allocation and more transparency for tenant members about the resources used.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2022-01-01\nValid as Of: 2024-04-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3087 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Updating HTML5 Apps Required\nDescription: Following this week's update of SAP Task Center, it is expected that the Task Center tile count will start showing Error. To restore the tile count, please update the HTML5 apps in the site manager of your central point of entry for accessing apps. For example, see central point of entry for accessing apps. For example, see Create a Task Center Tile for SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition.  . To restore theЕnd users might have to clear browser cache and refresh their browser. \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-19\nValid as Of: 2024-04-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3088 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Public Views Enabled\nDescription: You can now access public views, predefined by key users. For more information, see Working with Views", " browser cache and refresh their browser. \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-19\nValid as Of: 2024-04-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3088 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Public Views Enabled\nDescription: You can now access public views, predefined by key users. For more information, see Working with Views and Creating Public Views for End Users.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-19\nValid as Of: 2024-04-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3089 ---\nComponent: Application Autoscaler\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Metric Type cpuutil\nDescription: A new metric type called cpuutil (CPU utilization) is now available. This metric type is linked to the CPU entitlement usage of an application in Cloud Foundry, which depends on its size (memory). cpuutil allows users to set scaling rules based on CPU entitlement, such as scaling up if the usage exceeds 80% and scaling down if it falls below 40%.  Recommendation: If you use the cpu metric, we recommend you to switch to cpuutil to specify thresholds with values from 0% to 100%, which eliminates the need to calculate the CPU entitlement for your application.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 3090 ---\nComponent: Java Server\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Tomcat version for Java Web Tomcat 9 and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7\nDescription: Java Web Tomcat 9 (runtime version 4.75) and Java EE 7 Web Profile TomEE 7 (runtime version 1.173) have been updated to Tomcat version 9.0.87.   See the Changelog.  Recommended action: Update your applications to the latest runtime version.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-04-18\nValid as Of: 2024-04-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 541 ---\nComponent: Cloud Transport Management\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New build-runtime application service plan available.\nDescription: You can use the build-runtime service plan when you use SAP Cloud Transport Management as part of a service from the SAP Build ecosystem.  See:   Subscribing to Cloud Transport Management  Updating the Service Plan  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Application Development and Integration\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-02\nValid as Of: 2025-07-02\nVersion: 2506a\n\n--- Record 542 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Document Pricing - Clearing of Persisted Error Messages\nDescription: The persistent item-level messages used to be kept after item updates or repricing, resulting in incorrect calculation status. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-02\nValid as Of: 2025-07-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 543 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Ignore Inconsistent Condition Types During Condition Exclusion\nDescription: The condition exclusion based on the exclusion procedure was not functioning as expected when the condition types of an exclusion group were missing or inconsistent. The issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-27\nValid as Of: 2025-07-02\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 544 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Regular Upgrade\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services have been upgraded.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-01\nVersion: 28019\n\n--- Record 545 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Support for SAP extension schema for groups\nDescription: The default transformations of the following connectors support attributes from the SAP extension schema for groups, including application ID, type, and supported operations.  For more information, see  SAP Marketing Cloud  SAP Market Communication for Utilities  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-01\nVersion: 28019\n\n--- Record 546 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: IBM MQ Adapter Supports New Version\nDescription: A new variant (JMS Subscribe) for the IBM MQ Sender adapter (1.2.0) is available now.  See: IBM MQ Sender Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 547 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Support for SAP extension schema for groups\nDescription: The default transformations of the following connectors support attributes from the SAP extension schema for groups, including application ID, type, and supported operations.  For more information, see:    SAP Marketing Cloud  SAP Market Communication for Utilities  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 548 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Deep Links Support for Completed Tasks\nDescription: You can now open completed tasks directly using deep links.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 549 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extended Service Plan Migration Guide\nDescription: The service plan migration guide was extended with details on how to migrate to a lower-ranking service plan and additional steps you might need to consider when updating to another service plan. For more information, see Migrating to a Different SAP Task Center Service Plan.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-07-01\nValid as Of: 2025-07-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 550 ---\nComponent: SAP BTP Command Line Interface\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo,Other\nTitle: Discontinuation of Pre-2.61 Client Versions\nDescription: As announced on November 28th, 2024, we have now discontinued client versions older than version 2.61.  Action: If you are using a btp CLI client older than version 2.61, please update to the latest btp CLI client. Older versions can no longer be used.  To learn how to update your client, see Get Updates.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-26\nValid as Of: 2025-06-30\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_e3e6f2468803da5c1f73a7c61dec3c86bb25f4cc35dc01b90aab69f385e5101e_v2"}